From: BeeWi BC7PW bring-up <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] mt7601sta: mark the rate-switching region of MlmePeriodicExec()

Fourth instrumentation level, temporary. With 0011 applied the association-time
crash is gone and association now completes, but the maintenance timer dies a
moment later: PC is at MlmePeriodicExec+0x1d0, r4 (a pointer) holds 0x07060504
-- the bytes 04 05 06 07, MCS-index data -- and the faulting instruction is
ldrb r3, [r4, #0x290]. So r4 is being loaded out of an MCS index list.

The faulting PC resolves inside MlmePeriodicExec itself, not in the callee, so
these markers bracket what the 1 Hz timer runs and localise it to the region
between two of them:
  PEXEC 0-enter                  on entry (after the opening brace)
  PEXEC 1/2-before/after-apdrs   around APMlmeDynamicTxRateSwitching()
  PEXEC 3/4-before/after-drs     around MlmeDynamicTxRateSwitching()

Note the AP/P2P code is compiled in for this target, so the AP-side rate
switching runs too and is a live suspect alongside the STA side.
--- a/common/mlme.c
+++ b/common/mlme.c
@@ -851,6 +851,7 @@
 	IN PVOID SystemSpecific2, 
 	IN PVOID SystemSpecific3) 
 {
+	printk(KERN_ERR "PEXEC 0-enter\n");
 	ULONG			TxTotalCnt;
 	PRTMP_ADAPTER	pAd = (RTMP_ADAPTER *)FunctionContext;
 #ifdef ANT_DIVERSITY_SUPPORT
@@ -976,7 +977,9 @@
 	{
 #ifdef CONFIG_AP_SUPPORT
 		IF_DEV_CONFIG_OPMODE_ON_AP(pAd)
+	printk(KERN_ERR "PEXEC 1-before-apdrs\n");
 			APMlmeDynamicTxRateSwitching(pAd);
+	printk(KERN_ERR "PEXEC 2-after-apdrs\n");
 #endif /* CONFIG_AP_SUPPORT */
 #ifdef CONFIG_STA_SUPPORT
 		/* perform dynamic tx rate switching based on past TX history*/
@@ -991,7 +994,9 @@
 #endif
 					)
 				&& (!OPSTATUS_TEST_FLAG(pAd, fOP_STATUS_DOZE)))
+	printk(KERN_ERR "PEXEC 3-before-drs\n");
 				MlmeDynamicTxRateSwitching(pAd);
+	printk(KERN_ERR "PEXEC 4-after-drs\n");
 		}
 #endif /* CONFIG_STA_SUPPORT */
 	}
